# Build outputs are NOT committed. Approved 2026-10-08.
#
# The git history held 573 MB of .docx and 568 MB of .pdf against a working
# build folder of 86 MB, because the loop rebuilt and committed both books
# after every one of twenty units, and DOCX and PDF are already-compressed
# containers that git cannot delta. `.git` reached 1.4 GB; GitHub advises
# staying under about 1 GB. At 41 figures a unit the books roughly triple,
# so twenty more unit rebuilds would have added another 1-2 GB of history
# for files nobody reads from git.
#
# They are published as GitHub Release assets instead: free, 2 GiB a file,
# no bandwidth charge, outside git history. DOWNLOADS.md links them.
#
# An earlier `build/*.pdf` line here never took effect, because the files had
# been added to the index before it existed and `git add -A` keeps updating
# a tracked file whatever .gitignore says. Hence the explicit `git rm --cached`
# in the commit that landed this.
*.docx
*.pdf
*.zip
.*.md

# reference.docx is an INPUT, not an output: it carries the styles, fonts and
# section properties measured from the source book, and every build needs it.
!reference.docx
